	(gr_text "Seen from behind, the component side; up is up on the instrument.\nPut a 2 x 17, 2.54 mm socket on the front side, on the pins drawn on Dwgs.User: the board plugs onto\nthe display's GPIO header through the carrier.\nWith an 8.5 mm socket, parts up to 8 mm tall clear the rear cover ribs.\nOutline = the room inside the rear cover below its back holes, clear of the screw columns (drawn on\nDwgs.User with the inside of the cover).\nNo mounting holes: the socket holds the board, and the rear cover keeps it from backing off."
		(at 111.82 104 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
